@startuml usecase-core
title Use Case Diagram - Core Booking Flow (cumulative through Iteration 2)\nKorean Air Skypass Ticketing Reservation System

left to right direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam ranksep 60
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #555555
skinparam dpi 130

actor "Skypass\nMember" as Member
actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Payment\nGateway" as Pay <<external>>

rectangle "Korean Air Reservation System" {

  package "Authentication" {
    usecase "Register\nMember" as UC_Reg
    usecase "Login /\nLogout" as UC_Login
  }

  package "Booking" {
    usecase "Search\nFlight" as UC_Search
    usecase "Book\nFlight" as UC_Book
    usecase "Make\nPayment" as UC_Pay
    usecase "Issue\ne-Ticket" as UC_Ticket
  }

  package "Post-booking" {
    usecase "Look Up\nReservation" as UC_Lookup
    usecase "Cancel\nBooking" as UC_Cancel
    usecase "Process\nRefund" as UC_Refund
  }
}

Member --> UC_Login
Guest --> UC_Reg
Member --> UC_Search
Guest --> UC_Search
Member --> UC_Book
Guest --> UC_Book
Member --> UC_Lookup
Guest --> UC_Lookup
Member --> UC_Cancel
Guest --> UC_Cancel

UC_Pay --> Pay
UC_Refund --> Pay

UC_Ticket ..down.> UC_Pay : <<extend>>

note bottom of Pay
  External actor.
  Iteration 3 additions appear
  in the separate diagram.
end note
@enduml
